Below is an implementation-ready Montis command specification based on the command list from the prior turn. The user’s placeholder `[PASTE COMMAND LIST HERE]` was empty, so I scoped this to the listed Montis commands already surfaced: reports, calendar/workouts, activities, performance models, wellness/athlete data, communication, and the “what next” analytical command bank.

## 0. Global command-routing rules

Montis command dispatch must be deterministic. Do not infer or invent callable names. `run` is not a standalone command; it is only valid inside the four report function names: `runWeeklyReportV2`, `runSeasonReportV2`, `runWellnessReportV2`, and `runSummaryReportV2`. Any other use of `run` is invalid. 

The integration boundary is the Montis tool/CLI call, not a raw Intervals.icu REST endpoint. The provided specification names functions such as `readCalendarV1`, `writeCalendarV1`, and `getOneDayFullActivityV1`; it does not specify underlying Intervals.icu endpoint URLs. QA should therefore validate the Montis function call, parameters, mutation behavior, and rendered response, not an undocumented endpoint contract. 

When a command is ambiguous, route by intent family first: reports, calendar, activity, performance model, athlete/wellness, communication, or explanatory coaching. If required inputs are missing and the command would mutate data, ask before writing. If the command is read-only and a safe default exists, use the default and state it.

